  "notes": "Source: 2025-2026 Aultman College Catalog (Summer 2025), official Associate of Applied Science in Radiography curriculum plan (Fall — Semester One through Spring — Semester Five, 65 credit hours total), verified via aultmancollege.edu 2026-10-01. The catalog publishes the plan term-by-term; sequencing is cohort-based and courses must be taken in the published sequence per the program's progression policy ('Students are required to follow the curriculum plan sequence and meet all prerequisites for each course in the program'). Prerequisites and corequisites transcribed verbatim from the catalog's course-description section; the semester-one RAD trio (RAD 112 / RAD 114 / RAD 114c) and the lecture/clinical pairs (RAD 124+124c, 134+134c, 244+244c) are mutual corequisites in the catalog. Catalog graduation requirements: minimum 65 credit hours — 30 Foundational Education, 35 Radiography. The catalog notes that foundational education courses may be completed prior to entrance into the program.",
